WEBVTT

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:29.360
<i>Jean, Nadia and company find themselves on a desert island</i>

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:32.320
<i>where they are all living together.</i>

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:37.820
<i>Although they are living simply, peace does not last.</i>

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:42.120
<i>The cold war between Hanson and Sanson worsened.</i>

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:46.040
<i>So they decided on a fight to the finish using King.</i>

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:49.790
<i>But there is only one King.</i>

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.960
<i>As a lion, King is the king of the jungle</i>

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:54.840
<i>whom no other animal can beat.</i>

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:59.890
<i>So, using all his knowledge, Hanson made an iron King.</i>

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:04.970
<i>Sanson, however, failed to persuade King to run for him.</i>

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:07.350
<i>So he stole Hanson's iron King design,</i>

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:11.730
<i>and asked Jean to make an iron King for him.</i>

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:18.320
<i>The two Kings ran a race, but the result was in vain.</i>

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:23.740
<i>By the way, what secret does Nadia's Blue Water hold?</i>

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:36.670
Okay, Hanson!

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:38.130
Okay!

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:44.930
How is it?

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:47.060
It looks good.

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:48.810
Will you rev up the engine just a little more?

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:52.810
It sure is noisy.

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:54.020
What are you doing so early in the morning?

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:54.230
Keep quiet!

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:56.030
I can't sleep! It's disturbing!

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:58.070
Good morning, everybody!

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:00.200
Everyone, please gather round.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:02.120
We'd like to show you something nice.

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:13.460
Did you repair it?

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:15.920
We just have to patch the balloon,

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:17.460
and we can get off this island.

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:21.380
That's great! We can get back home at last!

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.180
This is good.

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:27.770
We won't eat together like this many more times.

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:31.940
Life here wasn't so bad all in all.

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:37.400
Clean air, the murmuring of a brook, birds singing.

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:40.860
Wow, you're very romantic today.

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:43.200
You sound like you're saying goodbye to this island.

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:45.740
Where do you intend to go?

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:52.080
West for two weeks will put us on Africa's east coast.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:53.420
Africa?

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:55.960
If we can be carried on the wind.

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:59.840
Thank you, Jean! I can go to Africa at last!

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:03.430
Are you so happy to go to Africa?

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:06.760
Africa is where I was born.

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:08.850
I don't care where it is.

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:13.390
I just want a town with better food and drink.

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:16.400
I'm sick of this food!

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:18.520
I see.

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:32.660
So many mosquitoes.

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:34.500
Marie feels itchy.

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:38.840
We'll get malaria with so many mosquitoes around.

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:40.340
Malaria?

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:44.970
I'll go ask Jean to make insect repellent.

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:48.510
In, over, under...

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:53.980
Why do I have to sew? I'm a man after all!

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:56.190
I quit! I quit!

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:57.610
Sanson!

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:01.690
He's impossible.

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:07.280
This world has two types of men, useful and useless.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:09.990
And you're the useful type?

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:15.500
Usually, a count like me would never work,

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:18.880
but I'm good at this kind of simple labor.

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:25.800
A mosquito was on your cheek.

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:28.390
Oh, a mosquito!

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:33.680
There are so many mosquitoes around here.

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:39.940
What are you going to do in Africa, Hanson?

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:41.860
Let's see...

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:46.570
The way our Senorita is now, we don't have anything to do.

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:47.820
Why's that?

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:53.490
We were bad guys who had our eye on Nadia's Blue Water.

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:55.660
But after we went aboard the Nautilus,

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:58.460
we became good guys again.

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:02.460
Because there is a far more evil person in Gargoyle.

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:04.590
What are you going to do, Jean?

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:09.090
I'm going to find the place where Nadia was born.

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:12.600
Doesn't she know her own birthplace?

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:17.730
She doesn't know where or when she was born.

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:22.060
I see. That's why she's a little eccentric.

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:24.730
How am I eccentric?

00:06:24.730 --> 00:06:26.280
N- Nadia...

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:29.950
Well, I didn't mean it that way!

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:33.370
Jean, will you come with me? Please?

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:34.620
Liquor?

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:38.870
What if everyone heard about it?

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:40.880
Where is it?

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:45.130
It's a little ways from here, a secret place.

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:53.140
I've created a natural wine by fermenting a wild vine.

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:54.390
Wine!

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:58.350
Right, something you could never get in any town.

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:00.900
A natural wine!

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:04.520
I didn't know we had such nice things on this island.

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:08.400
There are too many mosquitoes here to keep working.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:13.530
Well? How about it?
Shall we take a rest now?

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:17.450
How practical.

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:20.040
Well, what did you need me for?

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:27.250
Look! I'm being eaten alive by mosquitoes.

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:30.880
Don't you feel itchy?

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:35.550
Of course I do! But I don't want any scratch marks left.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:40.270
Please, Jean! Make an insect repellent for me.

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:43.810
I need sea mugwort for that.

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:45.820
Sea mugwort?

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:56.160
Good luck!

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:06.040
I wonder what Jean is doing?

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:09.260
He's been gone a long time.

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:12.720
Are girls so interesting?

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:15.970
I like machines better,

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:20.100
but Electra was a nice girl.

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:28.360
My Gratan!

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:34.910
Wait! Wait for me!

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:38.410
My Gratan!

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:50.920
What's this?

00:08:56.680 --> 00:08:58.390
Where is everybody?

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:02.060
Miss Grandis is out on a date with Ayerton.

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:03.730
A date?

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:06.100
They went to have some wine.

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:18.160
Stop! Stop! Stop! Stop already! My Gratan!

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:21.040
What?

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:21.990
A hole?

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:24.580
Yes, five large holes.

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:27.460
They open from the iron bottom.

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:29.960
How awful.

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:32.960
It looks like a submarine.

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:37.970
Apparently, this island is not an ordinary island.

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:44.390
It started to move while you were looking away?

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:45.560
That's right.

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:47.560
If someone was in it...

00:09:48.310 --> 00:09:49.690
Jean is with Nadia.

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:54.440
Wasn't Jean repairing the Gratan with you?

00:09:54.440 --> 00:09:58.070
Nadia came and took him away.

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:00.780
I see...

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:02.450
They're finally getting along.

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:07.500
But they shouldn't do it using my Gratan.

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:08.080
What?

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:09.960
Jean!

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:11.960
I've made the repellent.

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:14.090
Where is the Gratan?

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:16.090
What happened to the Gratan?

00:10:16.090 --> 00:10:19.390
Jean didn't steal it?

00:10:19.390 --> 00:10:21.850
Who in the world did then?

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:23.600
It's that fool Ayerton!

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:24.390
Ayerton?

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:27.770
You said he went to drink wine with Grandis?

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:30.400
Women are weak for material things, Sanson.

00:10:32.110 --> 00:10:33.650
Damn!

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:39.030
I couldn't make advances to her, even if I wanted to!

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:45.580
I didn't work day and night fixing my Gratan for them!

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:47.160
He'll be sorry!

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:01.300
Did you find them?

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:03.010
No.

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:05.680
Where did they go?

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:08.060
They must be in the woods.

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:09.770
But the Gratan's too large.

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:13.270
It's too troublesome to search on foot.

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:16.150
Let's wait for them till they come back.

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:17.190
Hanson!

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:18.280
What?

00:11:18.570 --> 00:11:23.780
Grandis is out for a drive with a man we don't know!

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:26.330
Who knows what he could be doing to her!

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:28.410
I won't ever forgive him,

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:30.410
even if the Queen of England did!

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:35.210
But we can't do anything without the Gratan.

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:36.130
Let's make one!

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:36.800
One what?

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:39.050
A machine to chase the Gratan!

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:41.220
A machine even better than the Gratan!

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:43.470
The Gratan II!

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:45.300
The Gratan II?

00:11:54.100 --> 00:11:56.070
I don't like grownups.

00:11:56.070 --> 00:11:57.110
Why not?

00:11:57.320 --> 00:12:00.440
There are lots of important things to do,

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:02.110
but they just keep wasting time.

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:06.990
We can't fix the balloon without the Gratan.

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:09.870
But they don't have to make that thing!

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:23.220
It's different than what I imagined.

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:27.100
We don't have time to come up with anything better.

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:30.850
How does it run? Don't tell me these pigs pull it.

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:31.390
That's right.

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:37.650
Let's put a horn on it. That'll make it look nice.

00:12:38.020 --> 00:12:41.530
Then it'll be too heavy to move fast enough.

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:45.530
Let's put wings on it. There will be less air resistance.

00:12:45.860 --> 00:12:49.790
Never mind its appearance! We have to hurry!

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:54.000
I'm really worried about what might happen to my Gratan!

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:57.630
I don't like this horrible style,

00:12:57.630 --> 00:12:59.250
but I'll put up with it to find Grandis.

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:00.250
Let's go!

00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:07.050
Not yet? Where is the wine?

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:08.600
Don't talk to me.

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:09.510
What did you say?

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:13.310
I can't do two things at the same time.

00:13:13.310 --> 00:13:16.060
Let's get my Katerine back quickly!

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:19.820
Sanson and the others will be pretty angry about this.

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:27.320
Go! Go, go, go!

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:32.290
How foolish! We're the only ones doing honest work.

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:34.040
But Marie's having fun!

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:36.420
I envy you, Marie.

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:40.540
I remember my days in the circus and just feel sad.

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:42.800
I'm taking a break.

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:44.050
A date with Jean?

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:47.050
No! I'm going to get some milk.

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:55.350
What happened? Have we arrived?

00:13:55.980 --> 00:13:57.390
It broke down.

00:13:57.390 --> 00:13:58.600
What did you say?

00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:00.980
It's not working.

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:04.820
Hanson just fixed it, and you broke it again.

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:05.820
It's not my fault.

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:09.660
I didn't break it. It broke by itself!

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:12.370
Move it!

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:20.880
Go, go, go!

00:14:24.130 --> 00:14:26.550
Let's go! Hurry up!

00:14:32.890 --> 00:14:35.430
Let's take a better road.

00:14:35.810 --> 00:14:41.940
Road? We're making our own roads!

00:14:42.270 --> 00:14:44.570
Let's go!

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:16.810
What are you doing?

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:21.900
I was just taking in the wash.

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:24.650
Didn't you go with Sanson?

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:28.650
The new vehicle is only for two people. So, I stayed.

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:32.820
Say, Jean, come with me.

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:37.240
I have something that I need to tell you.

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:39.500
Why are you so serious?

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:41.370
It's about our future.

00:15:41.710 --> 00:15:42.880
Our future?

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:48.920
I want you to come with me when we leave this island.

00:15:48.920 --> 00:15:52.630
Let me drink some wine first, and hurry up with it.

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:54.640
That was a lie.

00:15:56.220 --> 00:16:00.890
You mean you lied to me to make me come with you?

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:03.230
The important thing is what I'm going to tell you now.

00:16:03.230 --> 00:16:07.270
I lied to you for that very reason.

00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:10.650
So? Where do you want me to go?

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:11.990
To England!

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:14.870
To be precise, to my house.

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:17.200
To be more precise, I want you

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:20.580
as Count Ayerton Grenaban's wife,

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:22.830
to come to England with me!

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:27.670
Are you sure you haven't eaten it?

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:32.930
I'm sure! Everybody knows you'd get angry if we did.

00:16:32.930 --> 00:16:35.640
Angry? So in reality, you still want to eat it.

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:36.850
That's not true!

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:40.390
Sure it is! You ate it thinking I wouldn't know.

00:16:40.850 --> 00:16:45.060
You should have tethered it with a rope.

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:48.070
I couldn't do such a mean thing.

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:52.400
See? It serves you right.

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:54.530
I didn't eat it!

00:16:54.530 --> 00:16:56.700
What? This...

00:16:56.700 --> 00:16:57.990
What is it?

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:04.460
This is a great discovery!
We have to investigate this.

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:07.420
The island is on something very large.

00:17:07.420 --> 00:17:10.960
Hurry up and find my goat first!

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:12.460
That's...

00:17:20.560 --> 00:17:23.810
We've been looking for them a long time now!

00:17:23.810 --> 00:17:25.690
Shut up! You won't die!

00:17:26.060 --> 00:17:27.730
Are you sure?

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:29.860
What?

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:33.940
What's going on?

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:35.950
My poor Gratan!

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:39.450
Hanson, stop it!

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:54.920
It's my Gratan!

00:17:54.920 --> 00:17:56.470
We've found it.

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:02.390
Oh, my God!

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:06.230
You don't have to answer now. Just...

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:09.230
Shut up! Keep quiet! I don't believe people

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:13.400
who call themselves counts or nobles! Don't get any closer!

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:16.240
You'll see I'm a real nobleman in England!

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:32.840
Good! The real Gratan isn't broken.

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:35.340
My poor Gratan II...

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:42.930
I will always be there to protect you, no matter what!

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:44.220
You're too heavy!

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:45.470
Hold it right there!

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:51.270
Don't you ever touch my Senorita, or you'll be sorry!

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:56.320
Don't you ever touch my Gratan, or you'll be sorry!

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:06.160
This isn't a cave. It's a tunnel.

00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:10.920
I wonder who made this?

00:19:11.710 --> 00:19:13.790
Nobody seems to be using it.

00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:33.520
A dead end.

00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:37.280
Let's get back, Jean. It'll get dark soon.

00:19:37.280 --> 00:19:39.070
How can we open this?

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:42.910
Let's come back tomorrow. Everybody must be worried.

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:45.870
I suppose so. It'd be awful if we got lost.

00:19:45.870 --> 00:19:47.410
Let's get back, Nadia.

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:06.510
Hey, Headman!

00:20:06.510 --> 00:20:09.770
Don't say that. Please help me!

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:13.350
Reflect on your conduct by cooling your head.

00:20:13.730 --> 00:20:15.230
That's right, Headman!

00:20:15.610 --> 00:20:18.650
By the way, I haven't seen Jean and Nadia for some time.

00:20:18.650 --> 00:20:22.240
Where in the world are those two hiding?

00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:25.120
Jean is quite a knowledgeable boy, isn't he?

00:20:25.120 --> 00:20:25.990
Hanson!

00:20:27.990 --> 00:20:29.330
I'm cold.

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:30.370
It must be air conditioning.

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:31.160
Air conditioning?

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:39.130
What are these things?

00:20:45.430 --> 00:20:48.890
The ruins of a factory? There are so many chimneys.

00:20:48.890 --> 00:20:50.390
Could it be Gargoyle?

00:20:51.270 --> 00:20:51.890
No...

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:57.900
That looks just like the Nautilus.

00:20:58.270 --> 00:21:00.480
Why is it here?

00:21:00.480 --> 00:21:05.570
Why would someone leave a submarine hanging in the air.

00:21:05.570 --> 00:21:07.160
What is this place for?

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:12.160
We've lived on the same island as this all this time.

00:21:12.370 --> 00:21:14.620
We should get back quickly and tell everyone about this.

00:21:14.620 --> 00:21:16.460
It's a great discovery!

00:21:16.460 --> 00:21:19.630
But how can we get back? This walkway doesn't stop.

00:21:19.630 --> 00:21:24.130
Don't worry. We'll get out if we just keep going ahead.

00:21:24.130 --> 00:21:27.140
Why are you in such a good mood?

00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:30.430
You take everything too seriously, Nadia.

00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:33.890
You won't live long that way.

00:21:34.310 --> 00:21:35.390
I won't?

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:37.060
That's right, Nadia.

00:21:42.570 --> 00:21:43.320
What's this?

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:47.320
Yes, my name is Nadia.

00:21:47.700 --> 00:21:50.660
What is it? Who are you talking to?

00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:56.790
Oh no, Nadia! It's a dead end!

00:21:57.670 --> 00:22:00.540
Jean is my best friend.

00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:03.550
Oh no, Nadia's acting very strange!

00:22:05.090 --> 00:22:07.630
Nadia! Nadia!

00:22:09.010 --> 00:22:10.140
Nadia!

00:22:19.350 --> 00:22:21.480
Darn!

00:22:25.030 --> 00:22:26.070
It's okay.

00:22:48.720 --> 00:22:50.300
Nadia?

00:22:53.350 --> 00:22:56.350
Nadia!

00:23:12.780 --> 00:23:13.660
What's going on?

00:23:28.880 --> 00:23:31.180
Headman, you're not supposed to be out!

00:23:31.180 --> 00:23:36.680
Freedom! God must have helped me!

00:23:40.390 --> 00:23:41.390
What?

00:23:41.390 --> 00:23:42.440
What's that?

00:23:43.310 --> 00:23:44.860
It's an aurora!
